MotionBricks Studio

This project includes, adapts or downloads the third-party work below. The licence
texts it includes are in the licenses/ folder.


1. MotionBricks (https://github.com/NVlabs/motionbricks)
   Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES.
   Source code licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (licenses/Apache-2.0.txt).

   Files here that are derived from it, and changed from the originals:
     server/engine.py  numpy + ONNX Runtime port of motionbricks/model/soma/engine.py and
                       kernels.py, so the model runs without TensorRT or an NVIDIA GPU.
     server/bvh.py     BVH loader written to match motionbricks.io.bvh.
     server/quat.py    quaternion helpers written to match the maths the MotionBricks
                       runtime uses.


2. MotionBricks model and sample motion data (NOT included in this repository)
   setup.sh downloads the SOMA ONNX model and the BVH motion clips from NVlabs/motionbricks
   into ../motionbricks. They stay under NVIDIA's own terms and are not redistributed here.
   The motion clips are under the NVIDIA Sample Data Evaluation License
   (motionbricks/assets/motions/LICENSE.txt). It allows internal use to evaluate and test
   NVIDIA technology, and does not allow sharing the clips or works derived from them.
   The pose library (server/library.py) is sampled from those clips at run time.


